This package is a new extraction of Linux-visible seccomp policy and lifecycle
contracts designed for TheKernel and distributed under Apache-2.0.

Linux and TheKernel sources were consulted to understand observable UAPI,
verifier-profile, filter-stack, action, inheritance, and thread-synchronization
contracts.

Copied text: one excerpt. `src/action.rs` reproduces the action allow-list
switch at Linux 7.2.3 `kernel/seccomp.c:2069-2081` line for line, cited by the
prose around it. Its case labels are shorter than 40 characters, so a
40-character scan reports none, but the block is verbatim. That fragment is
GPL-2.0-only, (C) The Linux Kernel Authors; it is comment text, and no Linux
code is linked or compiled into this package. Nothing else in this package
reproduces upstream source text. See `docs/upstream-provenance.md`.
